<section class="section shell" id="faq">
  <div class="kicker">FAQ</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <details open><summary>Where is {d.fullName} located?</summary><p>{d.fullName} is located inside Iqbal Park in the Walled City of {d.city}, {d.region}, {d.country}, near {d.nearby1} and {d.nearby2}.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is {d.shortName} free to visit?</summary><p>Yes, {d.fullName} is a public national monument and is free to visit year-round. A small ticket may apply for some facilities within the surrounding Iqbal Park grounds.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is {d.fullName}?</summary><p>{d.fullName} is the national monument of {d.country}, built to commemorate the Lahore Resolution of 1940 that paved the way for an independent state.</p></details>
  <details><summary>When was {d.fullName} built?</summary><p>The foundation stone was laid on 23 March 1940 (the date of the Lahore Resolution), and the monument was completed between 1960 and 1968.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What are the best times to visit {d.shortName}?</summary><p>The cooler, clearer months from late October to March are the most comfortable. Mornings and after sunset are the most pleasant parts of the day in every season.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I reach {d.fullName}?</summary><p>It sits inside Iqbal Park in the Walled City of {d.city}. App-based ride-hailing or metered taxis can drop you near the park gates; the final walk to the monument is on foot through the park.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What other landmarks are nearby?</summary><p>Within walking distance you will find {d.nearby1}, {d.nearby2}, the Walled City of {d.city}, Wazir Khan Mosque and the Shahi Hammam.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is the weather like in {d.city}?</summary><p>{d.city} has a humid subtropical climate: very hot pre-monsoon summers (May–June), a warm monsoon (July–September), and mild, dry winters (December–February) that can bring seasonal smog.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is parking available at {d.shortName}?</summary><p>Designated car and motorcycle parking areas are available inside Iqbal Park; the narrow old-city streets around the Walled City fill up quickly, so allow extra time.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How much time should I plan for a visit?</summary><p>A focused monument-and-park visit takes about half a day; a full day lets you combine it with the Walled City, Badshahi Mosque and Lahore Fort.</p></details>
</section>

